## Design Section 2: FileUpload in Agent Mode

**Changes to `AgentPanel.tsx`:**

Add new props for tables, upload handler, and sample loader:

```typescript
interface AgentPanelProps {
  langfuseStatus: LangfuseStatus;
  tables: TableInfo[];
  onUpload: (file: File) => Promise<void>;
  onLoadSample: () => Promise<void>;
}
```

In the empty message area (currently lines 48-52), conditionally render `FileUpload` instead of the text placeholder when `tables.length === 0`:

```typescript
<div className="agent-panel__messages">
  {messages.length === 0 && (
    <div className="agent-panel__empty">
      {tables.length === 0 ? (
        <FileUpload onUpload={onUpload} onLoadSample={onLoadSample} />
      ) : (
        t('agentEmptyState')
      )}
    </div>
  )}
  {messages.map((msg, index) => (
    <MessageBubble key={msg.id} message={msg} messageIndex={index} />
  ))}
  <div ref={bottomRef} />
</div>
```

**Key behaviors:**
- `tables.length === 0` AND `messages.length === 0` → show FileUpload
- `tables.length > 0` AND `messages.length === 0` → show normal empty state text
- `messages.length > 0` → show messages (FileUpload hidden regardless of table count)
- If user deletes all tables and clears messages → FileUpload reappears
- Chat input remains visible below at all times

**Changes to `App.tsx`:**

Pass the new props when rendering AgentPanel (line 175):

```typescript
<AgentPanel
  langfuseStatus={langfuseStatus}
  tables={tables}
  onUpload={handleFileUpload}
  onLoadSample={handleLoadSample}
/>
```

No CSS changes needed — `FileUpload` will render inside the existing `agent-panel__empty` container which already centers its content.

